# ── Nebius Identity ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local dev only needs NOTHING from this file (see "Local dev" note at the bottom).
# Everything below is for deploying to Nebius.
# NEBIUS_IAM_TOKEN is a short-lived (~12h) USER token used ONLY for `docker login`
# and CLI calls during deploy. It is NEVER baked as a runtime endpoint env var —
# the endpoint authenticates at runtime via the service account below (NEBIUS_SA_*),
# which never expires. redeploy.sh refuses to deploy if NEBIUS_SA_* are unset.
NEBIUS_IAM_TOKEN=your_iam_token_here
NEBIUS_PROJECT_ID=your_project_id_here
NEBIUS_REGION=eu-west1
NEBIUS_SUBNET_ID=your_vpc_subnet_id_here

# ── Nebius Service Account (production auth — preferred over the IAM token) ──────
# The backend endpoint and the jobs it submits authenticate with a service
# account in production (IAM tokens expire every ~12h). Generate an authorized
# key pair, then base64-encode the private key PEM into NEBIUS_SA_KEY_B64.
# Leave blank for local dev or if you only use a short-lived IAM token.
NEBIUS_SA_ID=your_service_account_id_here
NEBIUS_SA_KEY_ID=your_authorized_key_id_here
NEBIUS_SA_KEY_B64=your_base64_encoded_private_key_pem_here

# ── Nebius Object Storage (S3-compatible) ──────────────────────────────────────
NEBIUS_BUCKET_NAME=archon-bucket
STORAGE_ENDPOINT_URL=https://storage.eu-west1.nebius.cloud
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=your_storage_access_key
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=your_storage_secret_key

# ── Nebius Managed PostgreSQL ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
POSTGRES_HOST=your_pg_host.mdb.eu-west1.nebius.cloud
POSTGRES_PORT=6432
POSTGRES_DB=archon
POSTGRES_USER=archon_user
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=your_pg_password_here
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://archon_user:your_pg_password_here@your_pg_host.mdb.eu-west1.nebius.cloud:6432/archon

# ── Nebius Inference API ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
NEBIUS_INFERENCE_BASE_URL=https://api.studio.nebius.ai/v1
NEBIUS_INFERENCE_API_KEY=your_inference_api_key_here

# ── Vision model (used by the extraction job) ──────────────────────────────────
VISION_MODEL=Qwen/Qwen2.5-VL-72B-Instruct

# ── Analysis model (used by the analysis endpoint agent) ──────────────────────
ANALYSIS_MODEL=meta-llama/Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct

# ── Container Registry ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
NEBIUS_REGISTRY=cr.eu-west1.nebius.cloud
# Registry path segment after the host (the deploy scripts read NEBIUS_REGISTRY_PATH).
NEBIUS_REGISTRY_PATH=your_registry_project_id_here

# ── Backend ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
BACKEND_HOST=0.0.0.0
BACKEND_PORT=8000
CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3000
# Firebase project that issues the ID tokens the backend verifies.
FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=your_firebase_project_id_here
# Set to "true" to bypass Firebase auth (local dev / headless smoke test only).
# docker-compose already sets this for you; never enable it in production.
SKIP_AUTH=false

# ── Backend TLS hostname (used only by nebius/redeploy.sh) ──────────────────────
# The backend serves HTTPS via Caddy `tls internal` (self-signed); DuckDNS just
# provides a stable hostname for the self-signed cert. Optional — leave blank if
# you front the endpoint a different way. redeploy.sh tolerates an empty token.
DUCKDNS_TOKEN=
DUCKDNS_SUBDOMAIN=archon-api
CADDY_DOMAIN=archon-api.duckdns.org

# ── Job runner backend (nebius | local) ───────────────────────────────────────
JOB_RUNNER_BACKEND=nebius

# ── Nebius extraction job image (on-demand CPU; vision LLM via Nebius Inference API) ──
EXTRACTION_JOB_IMAGE=cr.eu-west1.nebius.cloud/your_project_id_here/archon-extraction:latest
EXTRACTION_JOB_PLATFORM=cpu-d3
EXTRACTION_JOB_PRESET=4vcpu-16gb

# ── Nebius analysis job image (on-demand CPU, terminates on completion) ────────
ANALYSIS_JOB_IMAGE=cr.eu-west1.nebius.cloud/your_project_id_here/archon-analysis:latest
ANALYSIS_JOB_PLATFORM=cpu-d3
ANALYSIS_JOB_PRESET=4vcpu-16gb

# ── Compute preset failover ladder (resilient job provisioning, ADR-009) ──────
# Ordered, bounded list of `platform:preset` pairs tried IN ORDER when a job
# never provisions (terminal failure with zero instances / vanished job / quota
# precondition error). Each entry is tried at most once; when all fail the API
# returns HTTP 503 (not a silent stall). When UNSET, the ladder defaults to the
# per-job EXTRACTION_JOB_*/ANALYSIS_JOB_* preset above, then the next larger
# cpu-d3 size. cpu-d3 is the only CPU platform in eu-west1, so the real fallback
# is larger PRESET SIZES within it (Jobs quota can be granted per size).
# JOB_PRESET_LADDER=cpu-d3:4vcpu-16gb,cpu-d3:8vcpu-32gb
#
# OPT-IN GPU LAST-RESORT RUNG (OFF BY DEFAULT — leave commented unless needed).
# eu-west1 has exactly two platforms: cpu-d3 (CPU) and gpu-h200-sxm (GPU). You
# CAN append a GPU rung as a final emergency escape when every cpu-d3 size is
# quota-blocked — the ladder accepts any platform:preset pair. Example:
# JOB_PRESET_LADDER=cpu-d3:4vcpu-16gb,cpu-d3:8vcpu-32gb,gpu-h200-sxm:1gpu-16vcpu-200gb
# ⚠️ COST WARNING: an H200 preset is ~$4.50/hr vs ~$0.04/hr for cpu-d3. Archon
# jobs are CPU workloads — all LLM inference is remote HTTP to the Nebius
# Inference API, so the container NEVER uses the GPU. A GPU rung buys availability
# at ~100x the cost and burns money for zero compute benefit. Enable ONLY as a
# deliberate, temporary escape hatch, and remove it once cpu-d3 quota returns.
# How long (seconds) to probe a just-submitted job for a fast provisioning
# failure before returning it as pending. Keep generous so healthy-but-slow
# provisioning is never mistaken for a capacity miss.
# JOB_PROVISION_PROBE_SECS=30
# JOB_PROVISION_POLL_SECS=5

# ── Local dev ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# For `docker compose up --build`, the ONLY value you must set is
# NEBIUS_INFERENCE_API_KEY above — extraction and analysis call the Nebius
# Inference API for the vision/language models (there is no offline mock).
# docker-compose.yml supplies all the other local values itself: it points the
# stack at a local LocalStack S3, disables the cloud database, runs jobs as local
# containers (JOB_RUNNER_BACKEND=local), and bypasses Firebase auth (SKIP_AUTH=true).
# So you need NO Nebius infrastructure account (no Jobs/Endpoints/Storage/DB) — just
# an Inference API key. The browser UI at http://localhost:3000 still uses Firebase
# Google sign-in; point frontend/src/firebase.ts at your own Firebase project to use
# it, or just drive the backend API with scripts/test-pipeline.sh.
